.TH CALYPSO-PDF 1 "November 2026" "Calypso 1.0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
calypso-pdf \- PDF document viewer for GNOME (Calypso)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B calypso-pdf
[\fIOPTION\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Calypso reads PDF documents, annotates them, fills in forms, checks and adds
digital signatures, and offers tools to organize pages, merge, compress,
watermark, redact and protect documents with a password. Each document opens
in its own window; a document that is already open comes back to the front.
If Calypso is already running, the files are sent to the running instance.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-page =\fIPAGE\fR
Open at this page (number or page label).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-new\-window
Open a new window.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/calypso/settings.json
Preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/calypso/history.json
Recent documents, and the page, zoom and layout of each one.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/calypso/
Thumbnails of recent documents; copies kept for "Undo" after organizing pages.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CALYPSO_NSS_DIR
Certificate database used for digital signatures (default: the Firefox profile,
otherwise ~/.pki/nssdb).
.SH AUTHOR
Tof <nourpon@gmail.com>
